OrchardLinux kernel
===================

The kernel Orchard runs on iPhones and iPads with A7 to A11 chips: upstream
Linux v7.3-rc1 with the Apple A-series work on top. The 32-bit boards (A5 to
A6X) are on branch armv7.

The branch is upstream plus one merge commit per layer: drivers/<subsystem>,
devices/<chip>, configs. The work comes from HoolockLinux (Nick Chan),
Pauli1Go's iPad 7 and iPhone 7 tree (Paul Praschl), Berkay Kösebay's iPad 5
work and Orchard's contributors; every commit keeps its author.

Contributing
------------

Kernel work for Orchard is a pull request here, against main; the orchard
repository (https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard) holds no kernel patches.
The checks compile every platform of the branch with orchard's recipe and run
orchard's kernel tests. Build your branch with:

    orchard build --device <board> --kernel-tree <dir>

Commit style: AGENTS.md. Orchard builds the commit named in its
kernel/upstream.lock; a pull request there takes a newer one.

Upstream's README: Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst.
